  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone STI Policy Enhancement: Validating Open Science Policy, Implementation, and National Council Capacity Strengthening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bringing together science, education and research community of policy-makers, library communities of practice, IT practitioners and funders in the Sierra Leone open science ecosystem to review and validate the National open science policy for Sierra Leone. These workshops represents a pivotal step towards realizing the vision of a national open science policy and a national scientific publishing platform in Sierra Leone. It builds on the foundation laid by the LIBSENSE/SLREN Open Science Conference and the Sierra Leonean Writers Series, aiming to empower local researchers and scholars. Through this initiative, we envision a future where Sierra Leonean scientific knowledge is easily accessible and recognized globally, contributing significantly to the international scientific discourse.</narrative>
  </description>
